<?xml version="1.0" standalone="yes"?>
<!DOCTYPE PLUGIN [
<!ENTITY name      "stable-ipv6">
<!ENTITY author    "Lolig4">
<!ENTITY version   "2026.09.30">
<!ENTITY launch    "Settings/StableIPv6">
<!ENTITY gitURL    "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Lolig4/unraid-stable-ipv6/main">
<!ENTITY pluginURL "&gitURL;/&name;.plg">
<!ENTITY support   "https://github.com/Lolig4/unraid-stable-ipv6/issues">
<!ENTITY plgPATH   "/boot/config/plugins/&name;">
<!ENTITY emhttp    "/usr/local/emhttp/plugins/&name;">
]>
<PLUGIN name="&name;" author="&author;" version="&version;" launch="&launch;" pluginURL="&pluginURL;" support="&support;" icon="icon-network" min="6.12.0">

<CHANGES>
###2026.09.30
- Use the network icon of the settings page in the plugin list too.
- Versions are dates from now on.

###1.02.00
- Tell nginx, and optionally sshd, to rebind after the host address changed.
  Unraid binds them to the addresses present at service start, so they served
  the old one after a prefix change.

###1.02.00
- Have Unraid rebind its services after the host address changed, through the
  same update_services path its dhcpcd hook uses. They bind to the addresses
  present at service start and kept serving the old one after a prefix change.
- Coalesce the watcher events. One address change emits several lines and each
  of them used to trigger its own pass.

###1.01.01
- Lay the container suffixes out like the other fields and drop the help texts,
  which need a plug anchor to render and looked broken without one.

###1.01.00
- Give containers on the interface's macvlan network a fixed interface
  identifier, configurable per container in the settings page.

###1.00.00
- First release.

Note on the version format: versions are dates (YYYY.MM.DD, with a letter
appended for a second release on the same day). Unraid compares plugin versions
with strcmp, not version_compare, so every field keeps its fixed width.
</CHANGES>

<!-- Default configuration. The plugin installer never overwrites an existing
     file, so the settings survive an update and a reboot. -->
<FILE Name="&plgPATH;/&name;.cfg">
<INLINE><![CDATA[
@@stable-ipv6.cfg@@
]]></INLINE>
</FILE>

<FILE Name="&emhttp;/scripts/stable-ipv6">
<INLINE><![CDATA[
@@stable-ipv6@@
]]></INLINE>
</FILE>

<FILE Name="&emhttp;/scripts/apply">
<INLINE><![CDATA[
@@apply@@
]]></INLINE>
</FILE>

<FILE Name="&emhttp;/StableIPv6.page">
<INLINE><![CDATA[
@@StableIPv6.page@@
]]></INLINE>
</FILE>

<!-- Runs on install and on every boot, after the files above are in place. -->
<FILE Run="/bin/bash" Method="install">
<INLINE><![CDATA[
@@hook-install.sh@@
]]></INLINE>
</FILE>

<FILE Run="/bin/bash" Method="remove">
<INLINE><![CDATA[
@@hook-remove.sh@@
]]></INLINE>
</FILE>

</PLUGIN>
